# Page architecture

A **page** is composed of **sections**. A **section** is composed of **components**.

- Route files (`page.tsx`) only assemble sections — no large markup blobs
- Sections live in `src/app/(home)/sections/`
- Shared UI lives in `src/components/`
- Do **not** add `"use client"` unless the file needs event handlers, state, or browser APIs
- Prefer CSS (`:hover`, `details/summary`) over client JS for simple interactivity
- Do not extract a component that is used once and is under ~40 lines

```tsx
// page.tsx
export default function HomePage() {
  return (
    <>
      <SiteHeader />
      <main>
        <HeroSection />
        <ProductsSection />
      </main>
      <SiteFooter />
    </>
  );
}
```
